## Context

Post-merge review of PR #368 (0298). In `src/go/update.go` around lines
229-239, when a custom source is configured (`ERG_UPDATE_URL` or
`.ergrc [update] url`), the path of the blob to fetch is derived from the
*local* store layout, not from the source repository's layout. The shipped
`.ergrc` advertises pointing that key at git-erg itself; an adopter whose
store is `issues/` then asks git-erg for `issues/erg`, which does not exist,
and the command exits 0 silently. The `work-layout` test covers only the
`--upstream` arm, so nothing red catches it.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The blob path is derived from the local layout only when the source is
      a `trustedProjectOrigin`; otherwise the canonical `tickets/erg` is used.
- [x] A test mirrors `work-layout` for the custom-source arm: store `issues/`,
      source git-erg, and asserts the binary is fetched (red before the fix).
- [x] A missing blob at the source is reported, not swallowed into exit 0.
- [x] `make check` passes.
